## 11. Resource and performance requirements

The Windows machine should only manage connections and forward requests. It should not perform model inference.

Recommended initial constraints:

| Resource     | Design target                                                      |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Python       | 3.11                                                               |
| CPU          | Low background usage                                               |
| RAM          | Keep idle app overhead modest; target below 150 MB where practical |
| GPU          | No local inference or CUDA initialization                          |
| Disk         | Small application and logs; no model downloads                     |
| Network      | Stream requests rather than buffering full responses               |
| Processes    | One local app and one local proxy                                  |
| Remote model | Reuse the existing Kaggle server                                   |

These are engineering targets, not measured performance guarantees.

Avoid:

- Loading PyTorch on Windows.
- Downloading GGUF files to the laptop.
- Running a local model server.
- Polling Jupyter too frequently.
- Keeping unnecessary WebSocket connections open.
- Buffering large streaming responses.
- Starting duplicate Kaggle servers.

