python main.py model discover

# Check model server health
python main.py model health

# Start or reconnect the Cloudflare tunnel
python main.py tunnel connect

# Start the local forwarding API
python main.py bridge start

# Stop the local forwarding API
python main.py bridge stop

# Select access mode
python main.py mode direct
python main.py mode local

# Generate DSH provider configuration
python main.py dsh config

# Run compatibility diagnostics
python main.py test compatibility

# Export diagnostic information
python main.py diagnostics
```

Remote model stop/restart commands should not be enabled by default. They should require explicit confirmation and a separate safety check.

## 13. Development priorities and boundaries

The most efficient implementation order is not to build every module at once. It is to establish a reliable vertical slice first.

| Priority | Work                              | Reason                             |
| -------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| P0       | Existing Kaggle environment audit | Prevent accidental disruption      |
| P0       | Windows app foundation            | Establish stable architecture      |
| P0       | Jupyter connection                | Required control plane             |
| P0       | Existing model discovery          | Reuse the working server           |
| P1       | Direct endpoint                   | First usable remote inference path |
| P1       | Local Bridge                      | Second access path                 |
| P1       | Streaming and error handling      | Required for DSH                   |
| P0       | Structured tool-call verification | Essential for agent functionality  |
| P2       | Dashboard improvements            | Convenience                        |
| P2       | Ollama runtime                    | Optional expansion                 |
| P3       | GUI                               | Only after CLI is stable           |
| P3       | Executable packaging              | Final distribution                 |

The structured tool-calling investigation should run alongside the transport work. It must not be postponed until the end, because it could change the API compatibility architecture.

## 14. Risks and design decisions

| Risk                                  | Mitigation                                                  |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Kaggle session expiration             | Explicit session state and recovery instructions            |
| Existing server accidentally killed   | Discovery-first lifecycle; no automatic termination         |
| Duplicate model loads                 | Single-instance checks and reuse policy                     |
| Cloudflare URL changes                | Dynamic endpoint discovery and validation                   |
| API key exposure                      | Credential Manager and log redaction                        |
| Jupyter token exposure                | Separate control and inference planes                       |
| Tool calls returned as text           | Dedicated parser/template investigation and acceptance gate |
| DSH provider schema differs           | Verify installed DSH version before generating configs      |
| Streaming incompatibility             | End-to-end SSE tests                                        |
| Local proxy security issue            | Loopback-only binding and authentication                    |
| Tunnel works but model is unavailable | Independent tunnel and model health checks                  |

## 15. Final definition of done

The Windows application is complete only when all of the following are true:

1. It can securely connect to a Kaggle Jupyter Server.
2. It can identify the active Kaggle runtime and its GPUs.
3. It can detect and reuse the existing llama.cpp model server.
4. It can expose the model through a validated Cloudflare endpoint.
5. It can provide a localhost API through the Windows bridge.
6. Both modes use the same remote model server.
7. Streaming and error handling work correctly.
8. DSH can connect in either mode.
9. DSH receives actual structured tool calls.
10. DSH can execute tool results and continue its reasoning.
11. Kaggle disconnections are handled without unsafe process termination.
12. Credentials remain protected.
13. The application can be installed and launched reproducibly on Windows.

The most important architectural decision: Kaggle GPU Bridge should be a connection and management application, not another model-serving system. It manages access to the existing remote model; it does not duplicate it.

